2. Fix the missing route decorator
This is the first thing I would change.

In your uploaded program, you have:

def new_character(state: State) -> Page:

But you're using a button to navigate to "new_character".

Add @route above the function:

@route
def new_character(state: State) -> Page:
    state.fantasy_type = "Classic Fantasy"
    state.gender = "Woman"
    state.character_class = "Ranger"
    state.primary_ability = "Nature Magic"
    state.homeland = ""
    state.family_background = ""
    state.social_status = "Commoner"
    state.include_companion = False
    state.has_rival = False
    state.current_character = make_blank_character()

    return fantasy_type(state)

Why this matters:

@route tells Drafter that this function is a page the user can navigate to.

Your Create Another Character button depends on this route.

Your character_history list stays intact, so previous characters aren't lost.

